WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.850
Industrial cyber risk does not fit neatly into traditional information-security

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:05.320
assumptions.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:08.510
A loss of confidentiality may expose engineering information,

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:12.965
but a loss of system integrity or availability can also affect machinery, product quality,

00:00:12.965 --> 00:00:15.570
safety, environmental conditions, and essential services.

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:19.020
Security decisions must be evaluated against physical operations.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.740
OT environments combine specialized control devices, conventional computers,

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.485
industrial networks, safety functions, cloud services, remote vendors,

00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:27.605
and human operators.

00:00:27.605 --> 00:00:29.660
Equipment may remain in service for decades.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:33.020
Patching and architecture changes may require vendor support, testing,

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.485
maintenance windows, and carefully planned recovery.

00:00:35.485 --> 00:00:39.560
Without a common framework, each organization or supplier may define security differently.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:44.240
An asset owner may request a secure system without describing risk or acceptance criteria.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:48.130
A supplier may describe a component as secure without explaining its capabilities or

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:48.885
assumptions.

00:00:48.885 --> 00:00:52.740
An integrator may deliver a working process while leaving remote access and account

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:53.800
ownership unresolved.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.640
IEC 62443 creates a common language for these conversations.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.880
It connects business and operational risk to system requirements, supplier capabilities,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.520
service responsibilities, and lifecycle practices.

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:08.265
It encourages teams to define boundaries, identify required communication,

00:01:08.265 --> 00:01:12.585
select protection based on context, and preserve evidence that decisions were implemented.

00:01:12.585 --> 00:01:15.755
The standards also reinforce that cybersecurity is continuous.

00:01:15.755 --> 00:01:19.980
Operations change, software ages, vendors release updates, and threat conditions evolve.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.790
Security must be considered during design, procurement, integration, commissioning,

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:26.440
operation, maintenance, and retirement.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:31.610
IEC 62443 exists to make that shared work more consistent, accountable,

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:32.560
and suited to industrial reality.
